    "body": "> @mkruisselbrink so you'd have some kind of ephemeral storage?\r\n\r\nYeah, behavior (and implementation) wise this would be pretty similar to storage in anonymous iframes (If I understand the anonymous iframe proposal correctly, the desire for anonymous iframes to be able to access (ephemeral) storage is one reason they don't want the iframes to have opaque origins).",
