    "body": "The latest commit turns storage key into a tuple (with only one item for now) and uses its `origin` for the opaque origin comparison. Per the [tuple docs](https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#tuples) we can avoid using the indexing syntax if we name the tuple items, so I went with that approach.\r\n\r\nAlso, regarding https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/7567#discussion_r801790301, I'll plan to add a storage key comparison function in a separate PR unless you all prefer that it be a part of this one.",
